==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact eliminates the constraint that audit entries are immutable and complete. The AppendOnly assertion requires at least one audit entry with all required fields; clearing the fact allows Alloy to generate an empty AuditEntry or one with unset fields, violating the assertion.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrect  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows audit entries to have an actor role that does not match any real team membership. The AttributionCorrectness assertion requires every audit entry's role to be a snapshot of a genuine team membership; without this fact, the role can be arbitrary.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows tasks to exist without any audit entries. The AuditCompleteness assertion requires every task to have at least one audit entry; without the fact, Alloy can create tasks with no corresponding audit entries.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipExclusivity  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipExclusivity.als
    rationale: Removing this fact eliminates the constraint that every task has exactly one owner. The OwnershipExclusivity assertion checks this; without the fact, a task could have zero owners or multiple owners.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity
      - OwnershipExclusivity: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuthenticationRequired  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuthenticationRequired.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows tasks to be created without an authenticated owner and audit entries without an authenticated actor. The assertion requires one owner per task and one actor per audit entry; without the fact, these can be unset.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OneRolePerTeamPerUser  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OneRolePerTeamPerUser.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a user to have multiple roles in the same team, creating ambiguity in permission evaluation. The permission predicates assume a unique role per (user, team) pair; duplicate memberships would break the determinism of access checks.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

